- Improved performance of chunk loading/unloading, claim ticking, explosions and protection checks.
- Fixed fluids being able to flow into a claim from a different claim next to it.
- Fixed resized/upgraded claims counting loaded chunks twice, which kept their augments ticking after chunks unloaded.
- Bedrock players (Geyser/Floodgate) now see claim outlines and force field particles, as colored dust.
- Mixin audit now only runs in development environment, speeding up server startup.
- Fixed the claim lookup tree degrading on servers with claims spread far apart (int overflow in rtree-3i-lite volume math), making claim checks up to ~15x faster with many claims.
- Web map (BlueMap/Dynmap) player names and heads are now looked up in the background, instead of blocking the server on Mojang requests at startup and on claim changes. Markers aren't built at all without a web map mod.
- Endermen only check for Ender Binding claims when they would actually pick up or place a block.
- Pistons check claims once per push, instead of twice per moved block.
- Added an update checker: on startup (and every 12 hours) it checks this fork's GitHub releases and tells the console and admins when a newer version is out. `updateChannel` picks "release" or "alpha" (the latest development build), `checkForUpdates` turns it off.
- Added `autoUpdate` (off by default): dedicated servers download the new version, verify it against GitHub's checksum and install it when the server stops. The previous version is kept as a `.jar.old` backup, `autoUpdateBackups` sets how many are kept (1 by default).
- The /goml help GitHub link and the mod's contact links now point to this fork.
- Unknown or misspelled options in getoffmylawn.json are now logged with a suggestion (e.g. 'updatechannel', did you mean 'updateChannel'?), instead of silently disappearing from the file.
- Added `/goml admin update` to check for updates right away (and download them with autoUpdate on). `/goml admin reload` only checks for updates when the update options changed.
